@host = http://localhost:5069
@tunnel = https://YOUR-TUNNEL.devtunnels.ms
# {{phone}} comes from http-client.env.json.user (next to this file, ignored by git, never commit it):
#   { "dev": { "phone": "92XXXXXXXXXX" } }   <- put your real test number there
@verifyToken = YOUR_VERIFY_TOKEN

### App chal rahi hai ya nahi
GET {{host}}/

### Reminder bhejna
POST {{host}}/send-message?phoneNumber={{phone}}&medicine=Panadol

### Template reminder (24 ghante ke bahar bhi chalta hai). Template name/language Meta se match hona chahiye.
POST {{host}}/send-template/dose-reminder?phoneNumber={{phone}}&patientName=Ammi&medicines=Panadol 500mg, Disprin

### Webhook verify (sahi token)
GET {{host}}/webhook?hub.mode=subscribe&hub.verify_token={{verifyToken}}&hub.challenge=12345

### Webhook verify (ghalat token)
GET {{host}}/webhook?hub.mode=subscribe&hub.verify_token=ghalat&hub.challenge=12345

### Webhook POST (nakli message). /webhook now needs a valid X-Hub-Signature-256 header (401 without it).
### Meta signs the exact body bytes with your App Secret. To sign a test body in PowerShell:
###   $secret = "YOUR_APP_SECRET"   # same value as WhatsApp:AppSecret; never commit it
###   $body   = '{"entry":[{"changes":[{"value":{"messages":[{"from":"92XXXXXXXXXX","id":"wamid.TEST1","timestamp":"1700000000","type":"text","text":{"body":"le li"}}]}}]}]}'
###   $hmac   = [System.Security.Cryptography.HMACSHA256]::new([Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes($secret))
###   "sha256=" + [Convert]::ToHexString($hmac.ComputeHash([Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes($body))).ToLower()
### Paste the result into @signature, and the same $body (one line, no changes) as the request body below.
@signature = sha256=PASTE_SIGNATURE_HERE

POST {{tunnel}}/webhook
Content-Type: application/json
X-Hub-Signature-256: {{signature}}

{"entry":[{"changes":[{"value":{"messages":[{"from":"{{phone}}","id":"wamid.TEST1","timestamp":"1700000000","type":"text","text":{"body":"le li"}}]}}]}]}
